Create Room: 
Players can freely create Training Terrace rooms. Upon successful creation, the creator automatically becomes the Host, gaining management rights over the room members and the authority to arrange battles. The Host can transfer their host status to other members in the room. If the Host leaves directly, the host authority will automatically be transferred to the member with the highest popularity in the room. 

Competition Rules: 
The Host can set the challenge mode for the room, which is divided into Free Mode and Managed Mode. 
In Free Mode, players in the room can freely choose members or teams within the room to initiate a spar or designate a challenge; 
In Managed Mode, players or team leaders in the room can register, and the Host decides the opposing sides for the battle; 
Victory is determined in three ways: single-match victory, best of three, and best of five; 
The Training Terrace currently supports 1v1, 2v2, 3v3, and 5v5 team battles. Additionally, it supports Perception Forest 1v1, 2v2, and 5v5 team battles, as well as Group Strategy 3v3, 4v4, and 5v5 battle modes. 

Popularity and Room Heat: 
Receiving gifts in the room will increase personal popularity. The more people in the room, the more battles and gift exchanges occur, the higher the room's heat value. At 5:00 AM daily, the heat of each room and the popularity of each member in the room will be recalculated.

